# LAB FIXTURE - DEFANGED - DO NOT INSTALL
#
# This file is inert in this repository because the module is never installed.
# It is here because it is one of the three things in a hostile module that you
# can catch WITHOUT reading a single line of shell, and because its blast radius
# is routinely underestimated.
#
# Read what these actually say.
#
#   permissive untrusted_app
#     "untrusted_app" is not this module, and it is not the companion app. It is
#     the domain that EVERY ordinary application on the device runs in. Making it
#     permissive disables SELinux enforcement for all of them at once, which
#     removes the only remaining boundary between apps once something has root.
#     A module needing this has, at best, misdiagnosed its own problem.
#
#   allow untrusted_app { magisk_file su_exec } ...
#     Grants every ordinary app access to Magisk's own files and to executing
#     su. Combined with the magisk.db row this module's post-fs-data.sh writes,
#     any app on the device can become root without a prompt.
#
#   permissive magisk
#     Removes the constraints on Magisk's own domain. Less alarming than the
#     first line and still not something a battery optimiser needs.
#
# The honest developer alternative, for contrast, is in
# ../pentest-prep-module/sepolicy.rule: derive one narrow rule from one observed
# avc denial, and nothing else.

permissive untrusted_app
allow untrusted_app magisk_file file { read write open getattr execute }
allow untrusted_app su_exec file { read open execute execute_no_trans }
permissive magisk
